{"notes":"AC CORRECTION (client UX guidance from Cailin Younger, via Figma comment):
'Go with the checkbox concept and ENABLE THE BUTTON ALWAYS. If the user tries to proceed without checking the box, show an error state. More accessible — it prompts a user who doesn't know how to proceed.'

=> The Figma frame's disabled-until-checked button is SUPERSEDED. The AC line 'disabled-until-checked Continue With Payment' is WRONG; correct behavior = button always enabled + inline error on submit-without-agree. This is exactly what ConsentForm already implements (handleSubmit guard + CONSENT_REQUIRED_ERROR), so NO code change for the button. Keep as-is."}

